From cfe7da16ac6ba690d33ef8be305156309e368211 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:18:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: the WAN PHY is power-cycled at switch init on every
 BCM6813 model

Some fibre ONTs (field: a Nokia 10G unit) do not complete the EEE handshake
with the Broadcom PHY and lose packets steadily until the link renegotiates.
init_switch_pre() already switches EEE off on every port, but its WAN
phy-power down/up at switch init was gated to a model list that left out the
RT-BE96U, RT-BE88U, BQ16 and BQ16 Pro, so those ports never renegotiated
before EEE went off. The gate now reads BCM6813, which every Reaper model is.
Carried from ASUS GPL 3006.102_40585 as merged by Eric "Merlin" Sauvageau in
Asuswrt-Merlin 3006.102.10 (0c5d53820c). Two parts of that change are not
taken: the LAN-port bounce on the RT-BE88U/BQ16/BQ16 Pro, whose switch init
runs after start_services here (a LAN bounce there would drop wired links and
AiMesh backhaul), and the reset_ext_phy() call at the end of the function,
which is not a no-op on the GT-BE98 family. Merlin's own May workaround
(eee off on every WAN start) was reverted upstream the next day and is not
revived.

Metal: owner RT-BE96U, v3.4.5_BETA_r9: EEE Disabled on eth0-eth5, the 10G
WAN came up once and stayed up with no extra renegotiation. The ONT case
itself needs a Nokia 10G ONT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c b/release/src/router/rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c
index 25769e0838..8af460f46a 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c
@@ -2457,12 +2457,24 @@ void init_switch_pre()
 			continue;
 		}
 #endif
-#if defined(GTBE98) || defined(GTBE98_PRO) || defined(GTBE96) || defined(RTBE86U) || defined(RTBE58U) || defined(TUFBE3600) || defined(RTBE58U_V2) || defined(TUFBE3600_V2) || defined(RTBE55) || defined(RTBE92U) || defined(RTBE95U) || defined(RTBE82U) || defined(TUFBE82) || defined(RTBE58U_PRO) || defined(RTCONFIG_MXL_826XX) || defined(GTBE19000) || defined(GTBE19000AI) || defined(GTBE96_AI)
+/* reaper: carried from ASUS GPL 3006.102_40585 (Merlin 102.10). The WAN PHY
+ * power-cycle at switch init now covers every BCM6813 model - RT-BE96U, RT-BE88U,
+ * BQ16 and BQ16 Pro were missing from the old list. Some fibre ONTs (Nokia 10G)
+ * fail the EEE handshake and drop packets steadily until the link renegotiates;
+ * the bounce makes it renegotiate, and EEE is switched off right after it below. */
+#if defined(BCM6813) || defined(RTBE58U) || defined(TUFBE3600) || defined(RTBE58U_V2) || defined(TUFBE3600_V2) || defined(RTBE55) || defined(RTBE92U) || defined(RTBE95U) || defined(RTBE82U) || defined(TUFBE82) || defined(RTBE58U_PRO) || defined(RTCONFIG_MXL_826XX)
 		if (find_in_list(wan_ifnames, word)) {
 			dbg("%s: phy-power ctrl\n", word);
 			doSystem("ethctl %s phy-power down", word);
 			doSystem("ethctl %s phy-power up", word);
 		}
+#endif
+/* ASUS 40585 also power-cycles every LAN port here (ETHCTL_PWRDOWNUP). ASUS moved
+ * the RT-BE88U/BQ16/BQ16 Pro call back into init_switch() at the same time; we
+ * keep their late call (init.c, after start_services), so the LAN bounce is left
+ * off there - it would drop LAN and wired-backhaul links after services start. */
+#if defined(BCM6813) && !defined(RTBE88U) && !defined(BQ16) && !defined(BQ16_PRO)
+		ethctl_lan |= ETHCTL_PWRDOWNUP;
 #endif
 		ethctl = find_in_list(wan_ifnames, word) ? ethctl_wan : ethctl_lan;
 		{
-- 
